# First Horde skeletal horse from Zachariah Post (Brill).
# Sources: Forever client 1.60.1.70338 tables via wago.tools (ItemSparse: level,
# price, races, riding spell; SkillLineAbility: Riding); npcs.json and
# items.json for the trainer, the vendor and its stock.
# Forever riding: the client files every racial riding spell under one Riding
# skill (SkillLineAbility), so any riding trainer of your faction teaches it:
# Apprentice Riding (skill 75) from level 40, Journeyman Riding (150) at 60.
# Blizzard: learning to ride grants a mount, and training costs 100g at 40 and
# 1,000g at 60 (Kris Zierhut). ItemSparse lists the
# mounts at 20g (level 40) and 200g (level 60), usable by every race of the
# faction; whether a vendor still wants Exalted with another race's city (the
# Era rule) is server-side and unconfirmed.

step Learn to ride
  zone Tirisfal Glades
  tip Velma Warnam and Zachariah Post's stable are in Brill, Tirisfal Glades. At 40 Velma Warnam teaches Riding (100g per Blizzard's designers), and learning it gives you a mount. The Forever client lets every Horde race ride these.
  level 40
  train 4773                          -- Velma Warnam, riding trainer
  skill Riding 75

step Pick a colour
  tip Zachariah Post sells the other colours (20g each in the Forever client). Buy any you want, or none if the mount you were given is the one you like.
  vendor 4731                         -- Zachariah Post
  buy 13331 npc 4731 optional         -- Red Skeletal Horse, 20g
  buy 13332 npc 4731 optional         -- Blue Skeletal Horse, 20g
  buy 13333 npc 4731 optional         -- Brown Skeletal Horse, 20g
  note Black Skeletal Horse is a new Forever horse (level 40) whose source is not known yet.
